{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lemuroid-compliant-hoopoe","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nA normal post-merge `review-plan` from the project checkout made zero LLM calls and took 512.139s before failing because `git fetch origin` hit the 300s timeout. The checkout is partial/promisor (`blob:none`) and its `origin.fetch` maps every remote head. Attested ref resolution calls `fetch_origin()` without a ref, which executes `git fetch --quiet --no-filter origin`; this can traverse/materialize the enormous tickets history while only a code SHA is needed. The failed attempt left partial packs, including one approximately 153.6 MB.\n\nA normal retry from a temporary clone whose origin fetch refspec was main-only crossed the fetch boundary and completed the same review with signed PASS. This discriminates broad-ref transfer from model latency. It is distinct from `strained-bare-turnstone`, which addressed intermittent transport stalls and durable voting behavior, and from `grassy-cracked-morpho`, which covers completion close history-times-tracker scanning.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce attested resolution from a partial/promisor checkout whose origin fetch refspec includes both code and the large tickets branch.\n- Change snapshot ref materialization to fetch only the requested code ref/object while preserving fail-closed attestation semantics and support for remote refs.\n- Preserve blob materialization when the requested snapshot requires it without broadening the remote refspec.\n- Add a regression test that records the exact fetch argv/refspec and rejects an unscoped no-filter origin fetch.\n- Measure the fetch boundary before and after with a representative main-only target.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Resolving a specific attested code ref does not fetch unrelated origin heads.\n- [ ] Blobless/promisor checkouts can still materialize the requested snapshot when required.\n- [ ] Missing or unreachable requested refs continue to fail closed.\n- [ ] Tests pin scoped fetch arguments and cover a checkout with an unrelated large branch.\n- [ ] Before/after fetch duration and transferred-object evidence are recorded.\n- [ ] No LLM, gate, or tracker behavior is bypassed.","id":"39a2-4832-e436-4850","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["performance","plan-review","git","snapshot"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Attested ref materialization broad-fetches all origin heads"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787542691850644001,"uuid":"42058d0b-d70a-4e2e-ac25-d44179433a24"}